{% doc %}
  @description
  This snippet renders video controls for video(s) with the class specified in "video_class".
  If there is more than one video with this class (such as when using the core-video snippet with mobile/desktop videos),
  the snippet detects which video is visible and controls only that one, muting and pausing the hidden video.

  Accepts:

  @param {string} class - Class of the video controls container
  @param {string} video_class - The video class of a single or multiple videos. E.g: "js-hero-video--[UID]" - ensure that this class is unique by adding a section.id or something similar
  @param {boolean} has_mute - Renders mute/unmute buttons
  @param {boolean} has_pause - Renders pause/play buttons
  @param {boolean} scroll_autoplay - Autoplay the visible video(s) when it is scrolled into view.
  @param {boolean} play_on_click_video - Toggles play/pause when the video element is clicked
  @param {boolean} hide_button_on_play - Hides the play button on play
  @param {boolean} pause_page_videos_on_play - Pauses all videos on the page when playing this video
  @param [intersection_threshold] - Supports {Number | String(Number[])} - The trigger thresholds for scroll_autoplay intersection observer.

  It is important to ensure that the "video_class" passed to this snippet is unique for each section or context where
  the snippet is used.

  For example, you can generate a unique class using the section ID:

  @example
  {% assign video_class = "js-hero-video--" | append: section.id %}
  {% render 'core-video',
    class: video_class
    ...
  %}
  {% render 'core-video-controls',
    video_class: 'js-video-class'
    has_mute: true
    has_pause: false
  %}
{% enddoc %}

